  "policy": [
    "One vehicle per source owner. Select an admitted index uniformly within each owner; use identical energy, joint rates, home power and power laws for both generators.",
    "The Poisson control is rerun on this bank. Older pilot energy results use different selected parameters and are not this paired control.",
    "Availability rule: independently choose the next context using joint-rate shares; after the previous charge ends add an exponential idle gap, then sample uniformly within the remaining part of the first permissible window.",
    "This changes the timing process and its marginal within-window start distribution. A chosen next context can require waiting even if another context has an earlier window.",
    "Internal calibration adjusts only the idle-gap mean to a finite-prefix throughput proxy, N completions divided by elapsed hours from an empty clock. It is not empirical fitting or proof of a stationary mean.",
    "The same calibration event prefix is reused during bracketing/bisection. Verification and study use separate owner/replicate/component hash streams; their outcomes never tune the idle mean or select parameter indices.",
    "A zero-idle prefix below target is a limitation of this policy/path proxy, not proof of physical impossibility. Retain the owner at zero idle with a review flag; do not redraw or exclude it.",
    "The 0.2% calibration proxy tolerance and 5% verification band are development diagnostics, not statistical confidence limits or production acceptance criteria. Review owner rows as well as pooled totals.",
    "Study starts and literal completions in [0, study_hours) are reported separately. Warm-up starts can complete during study; sessions starting in study may finish afterwards.",
    "Availability sessions are constructed without overlap; zero rejection is not evidence that completed frequency matches target. This is paired on owner parameters, not on candidate events.",
    "Keep the constant E/P energy proxy, fixed owner usual energy and home power, and per-session non-home power. No battery clipping, added driving energy, conversion losses, site queues or dwell constraints are introduced.",
    "Paired energy MCSE describes the small conditional pilot over the saved bank and process streams. Input-fit uncertainty, initialization stationarity, empirical validation and production precision remain unresolved."
